@page "/"

<PageTitle>CRM Ticketing</PageTitle>

<h1>CRM Ticketing System</h1>

<p class="lead">
    Blazor WebAssembly client for the CRM ticketing API. This project is built with
    spec-driven development: every feature starts as a story intake, becomes a plan,
    and only then becomes code.
</p>

<div class="alert alert-secondary" role="alert">
    <strong>Scaffold state.</strong> No domain features are implemented yet. The
    ticketing and CRM scope is defined in
    <code>.squad/stories/</code> and planned into <code>.squad/plans/</code>
    before any of it is written.
</div>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">Where things live</h2>
<ul>
    <li><code>src/CrmTicketing.Domain</code> — entities, value objects, invariants. No framework dependencies.</li>
    <li><code>src/CrmTicketing.Shared</code> — request/response contracts shared by client and API.</li>
    <li><code>src/CrmTicketing.Infrastructure</code> — persistence and external integrations.</li>
    <li><code>src/CrmTicketing.Api</code> — HTTP surface, controllers, composition root.</li>
    <li><code>src/CrmTicketing.Client</code> — this app: pages, components, typed API clients.</li>
</ul>

<p>
    Use <a href="diagnostics">Diagnostics</a> to confirm the client can reach the API.
</p>
